cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LIBRAIN in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LIBRAIN: A Multi-Agent RAG System for Scientific Discovery"
abstract: >-
  LIBRAIN is an open-source, auditable multi-agent retrieval-augmented
  generation system for scientific hypothesis discovery, built on .NET 10.
  It ingests arXiv PDFs into a Qdrant vector index and runs three pipelines:
  citation-grounded synthesis, an extrapolative Discovery Mode that fences
  speculative content into a labelled novelClaim field, and two ablation
  baselines. A structural citation-validation contract guarantees zero
  fabricated chunk references by construction, and every stage emits
  correlation-ID-keyed audit events.
